<StandaloneVideo>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "published": true,
  "game_id": 54,
  "created_at": "2026-03-30T18:20:54.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 63,
  "properties": {
    "video_key": "pl-aif2-filtering-data-u3",
    "instructions_important": "false",
    "skip_dialog": true,
    "skip_sound": true,
    "parent_level_id": 28811,
    "name_suffix": "_24",
    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Supporting Students with Web Lab Levels\r\n<div style=\"width: 100%; max-width: 760px; margin: 20px auto; border: 0px solid #B7E0E5; background-color: #FFFFFF;\">\r\n\r\n<div style=\"padding: 25px 35px 10px 35px;\">\r\n    <p style=\"font-size: 14pt;  line-height: 1.3; margin: 0 0 22px 0;\">\r\n      This stucture outlines a simple process you can use to support students as they work with AI to understand, modify, and improve existing code.\r\n    </p>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px 14px; margin: 18px 0 8px 0;\">\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 20pt; margin: 0;\">🔍 Understand the Starter Code</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <p style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0 0 18px 8px;\">\r\n      Help students first make sense of what’s already there. Encourage them to identify what the code is doing before trying to change it.\r\n    </p>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px 14px; margin: 18px 0 8px 0;\">\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 20pt; margin: 0;\">📌 Locate the TODO in the Comments</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <p style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0 0 18px 8px;\">\r\n      Direct students to the TODO sections, which highlight exactly where changes or additions need to be made.\r\n    </p>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px 14px; margin: 18px 0 8px 0;\">\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 20pt; margin: 0;\">🧠 Plan the Behavior (in words)</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <p style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0 0 18px 8px;\">\r\n      Before jumping into code, have students describe what they want the program to do in plain language. This builds clarity and intention.\r\n    </p>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px 14px; margin: 18px 0 8px 0;\">\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 20pt; margin: 0;\">🤖 Prompt the AI (ROPE)</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <p style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0 0 18px 8px;\">\r\n      Support students in writing a clear prompt using structure: Role, Objective, Parameters, Expectations, or your updated framework, so the AI can generate useful code.\r\n    </p>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 8px; padding: 8px 14px; margin: 18px 0 8px 0;\">\r\n      <p style=\"font-size: 20pt; margin: 0;\">🔁 Test and Refine</p>\r\n    </div>\r\n    <p style=\"font-size: 13pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0 0 18px 8px;\">\r\n      Encourage students to run their code, check if it works, and make improvements. Iteration is key. Students should expect to adjust both their code and their prompts.\r\n    </p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background-color: #026C7A; color: #FFFFFF; padding: 8px 35px;\">\r\n    <p style=\"font-size: 11pt; font-style: italic; font-weight: bold; margin: 0;\">\r\n      Start with understanding the code, plan the behavior, prompt the AI, and refine through testing.\r\n    </p>\r\n  </div>\r\n\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n## Try it out\r\n\r\n#### Watch the video below to see the process in action. This video walks through the steps of the following activity. "
  },
